  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Adsorption is process where randomness decreases and energy is released. Hence, <math> <mrow> <mtext>ΔS</mtext></mrow> </math> will be negative (as randomness is decreasing) and <math> <mrow> <mtext>ΔH</mtext></mrow> </math> will also be negative (<math> <mrow> <mtext>ΔH</mtext></mrow> </math> is negative for exothermic processes).<br />Depending on the values of Entropy and enthalpy, the Gibbs energy can either be negative or positive.",
